Relevant columns and potential usage  
• GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES.GEO_US_CENSUS_PLACES.PLACES_PENNSYLVANIA  
  – "place_name": filter to Philadelphia.  
  – "place_geom": polygon (WKB) that outlines each place – used with ST_CONTAINS / ST_DISTANCE.  

• GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_FEATURES_POINTS  
  – "geometry": point (WKB) representing every mapped object – turn into GEOMETRY/GEOGRAPHY for distance work.  
  – "all_tags": VARIANT list holding every OSM tag – flatten to find tag_key = 'amenity' and tag_value ∈ ('library','place_of_worship','community_centre').  
  – "osm_id","osm_version","osm_timestamp": book‑keeping / uniqueness.  

Useful conditions  
1. p."place_name" ILIKE '%Philadelphia%' – unique boundary row.  
2. f.value:"key"::STRING = 'amenity'.  
3. f.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ('%library%','%place%worship%','%community%centre%').  
4. ST_CONTAINS( ST_GEOMFROMWKB(pl."place_geom"), ST_GEOMFROMWKB(pt."geometry") ) – point lies in Philadelphia.  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL statements (each limited to 20 rows, all identifiers in double‑quotes).  

```sql
-- 1. Description: Look at the basic Philadelphia record in the Census Places table.
SELECT *
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES"."GEO_US_CENSUS_PLACES"."PLACES_PENNSYLVANIA"
WHERE "place_name" ILIKE '%Philadelphia%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Inspect only the polygon (in WKT) and name for Philadelphia.
SELECT "place_name",
       ST_ASWKT(ST_GEOMFROMWKB("place_geom")) AS "phila_wkt"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES"."GEO_US_CENSUS_PLACES"."PLACES_PENNSYLVANIA"
WHERE "place_name" = 'Philadelphia'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Sample raw point rows so we can see tag structure.
SELECT "osm_id",
       "all_tags"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_FEATURES_POINTS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: List the distinct tag keys that exist in PLANET_FEATURES_POINTS.
SELECT DISTINCT f.value:"key"::STRING AS "tag_key"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_FEATURES_POINTS" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( INPUT => t."all_tags" ) f
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: List distinct amenity values (libraries, worship places, etc.).
SELECT DISTINCT f.value:"value"::STRING AS "amenity_value"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_FEATURES_POINTS" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( INPUT => t."all_tags" ) f
WHERE f.value:"key"::STRING = 'amenity'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Show 20 library points that fall inside Philadelphia’s boundary.
SELECT pt."osm_id",
       ST_ASWKT(ST_GEOMFROMWKB(pt."geometry")) AS "pt_wkt"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_FEATURES_POINTS" pt,
     "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES"."GEO_US_CENSUS_PLACES"."PLACES_PENNSYLVANIA" pl,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( INPUT => pt."all_tags" ) f
WHERE pl."place_name" = 'Philadelphia'
  AND f.value:"key"::STRING = 'amenity'
  AND f.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE '%library%'
  AND ST_CONTAINS(
        ST_GEOMFROMWKB(pl."place_geom"),
        ST_GEOMFROMWKB(pt."geometry")
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Retrieve worship places in Philadelphia with timestamp.
SELECT pt."osm_id",
       pt."osm_timestamp",
       ST_ASWKT(ST_GEOMFROMWKB(pt."geometry")) AS "pt_wkt"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_FEATURES_POINTS" pt,
     "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES"."GEO_US_CENSUS_PLACES"."PLACES_PENNSYLVANIA" pl,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( INPUT => pt."all_tags" ) f
WHERE pl."place_name" = 'Philadelphia'
  AND f.value:"key"::STRING = 'amenity'
  AND f.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE '%place%worship%'
  AND ST_CONTAINS(
        ST_GEOMFROMWKB(pl."place_geom"),
        ST_GEOMFROMWKB(pt."geometry")
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Pull community centres in Philadelphia (distinct IDs).
SELECT DISTINCT pt."osm_id"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_FEATURES_POINTS" pt,
     "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES"."GEO_US_CENSUS_PLACES"."PLACES_PENNSYLVANIA" pl,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( INPUT => pt."all_tags" ) f
WHERE pl."place_name" = 'Philadelphia'
  AND f.value:"key"::STRING = 'amenity'
  AND f.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE '%community%centre%'
  AND ST_CONTAINS(
        ST_GEOMFROMWKB(pl."place_geom"),
        ST_GEOMFROMWKB(pt."geometry")
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Combine all three amenity types and list with their type label.
SELECT pt."osm_id",
       f.value:"value"::STRING AS "amenity_type",
       ST_ASWKT(ST_GEOMFROMWKB(pt."geometry")) AS "pt_wkt"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_FEATURES_POINTS" pt,
     "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES"."GEO_US_CENSUS_PLACES"."PLACES_PENNSYLVANIA" pl,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( INPUT => pt."all_tags" ) f
WHERE pl."place_name" = 'Philadelphia'
  AND f.value:"key"::STRING = 'amenity'
  AND f.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ( '%library%', '%place%worship%', '%community%centre%' )
  AND ST_CONTAINS(
        ST_GEOMFROMWKB(pl."place_geom"),
        ST_GEOMFROMWKB(pt."geometry")
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--10. Description: Illustrative query that computes pairwise distances between the first 20 amenities
--                 inside Philadelphia and returns the shortest one (sample only).
WITH phila AS (
  SELECT ST_GEOMFROMWKB(pl."place_geom") AS "poly"
  FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES"."GEO_US_CENSUS_PLACES"."PLACES_PENNSYLVANIA" pl
  WHERE pl."place_name" = 'Philadelphia'
  LIMIT 1
),
amenities AS (
  SELECT pt."osm_id",
         ST_GEOMFROMWKB(pt."geometry") AS "geom"
  FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_FEATURES_POINTS" pt,
       phila,
       LATERAL FLATTEN( INPUT => pt."all_tags" ) f
  WHERE f.value:"key"::STRING = 'amenity'
    AND f.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ( '%library%', '%place%worship%', '%community%centre%' )
    AND ST_CONTAINS( (SELECT "poly" FROM phila), ST_GEOMFROMWKB(pt."geometry") )
  LIMIT 20
)
SELECT a1."osm_id"  AS "amenity_id_1",
       a2."osm_id"  AS "amenity_id_2",
       ST_DISTANCE(a1."geom", a2."geom") AS "distance_meters"
FROM amenities a1
JOIN amenities a2
  ON a1."osm_id" < a2."osm_id"
ORDER BY "distance_meters"
LIMIT 20;
```

The ten queries progress from inspecting Philadelphia’s boundary, exploring the OpenStreetMap tag structure, filtering for relevant amenities, to a final illustrative distance calculation sample—each capped at 20 rows for quick exploration.
